REAL-WORLD FORM EXAMPLE

================================================================================

export default function Form() {

  const handleSubmit = (e) => {

    e.preventDefault();

    console.log('Form submitted');
  };

  return (
    <form onSubmit={handleSubmit}>

      <label htmlFor="username">
        Username:
      </label>

      <input
        id="username"
        type="text"
        onChange={(e) =>
          console.log(e.target.value)
        }
      />

      <button type="submit">
        Submit
      </button>

    </form>
  );
}

Important Parts
Code                  | Purpose
----------------------|--------------------------------------
onSubmit              | Handles form submission
e.preventDefault()    | Prevents normal browser form submission
htmlFor               | Associates label with input
onChange              | Handles input changes
e.target.value        | Current input value


