Example 2: Conditional Rendering with Ternary Operator

================================================================================

import { useState } from 'react';

export default function LoginStatus() {

  const [isLoggedIn, setIsLoggedIn] =
    useState(false);

  return (
    <div>

      {isLoggedIn ? (
        <h1>Welcome back, Alice!</h1>
      ) : (
        <h1>Please log in</h1>
      )}

      <button
        onClick={() =>
          setIsLoggedIn(!isLoggedIn)
        }
      >
        {isLoggedIn ? 'Logout' : 'Login'}
      </button>

    </div>
  );
}

Ternary Syntax
condition ? valueWhenTrue : valueWhenFalse


Applied here:

isLoggedIn = false

Heading → Please log in
Button  → Login


isLoggedIn = true

Heading → Welcome back, Alice!
Button  → Logout


