Example 3: List Rendering with map()

================================================================================

export default function TodoList() {

  const todos = [
    {
      id: 1,
      text: 'Learn React',
      completed: false
    },
    {
      id: 2,
      text: 'Build a project',
      completed: true
    },
    {
      id: 3,
      text: 'Deploy app',
      completed: false
    }
  ];

  return (
    <div>

      <h1>My Todos</h1>

      <ul>

        {todos.map(todo => (

          <li key={todo.id}>

            <span
              style={{
                textDecoration:
                  todo.completed
                    ? 'line-through'
                    : 'none'
              }}
            >
              {todo.text}
            </span>

          </li>

        ))}

      </ul>

    </div>
  );
}

Code Explanation
Code / Concept             | Purpose
---------------------------|--------------------------------------------
todos.map(...)             | Converts each todo into JSX
todo                       | Current todo object
key={todo.id}              | Gives item stable identity among siblings
{todo.text}                | Displays todo text
todo.completed             | Checks completion status
textDecoration             | Dynamically applies strikethrough

Understanding Inline Styles
style={{
  textDecoration:
    todo.completed
      ? 'line-through'
      : 'none'
}}

First { }   → Enter JavaScript expression
Second { }  → JavaScript object


Output:

My Todos

- Learn React
- Build a project    ← strikethrough
- Deploy app


