================================================================================

ONE-LINE INTERVIEW ANSWER

================================================================================

JSX is a JavaScript syntax extension used to describe React UI in an HTML-like form. When state or props change, React renders the new UI description, reconciles it with the previous result, and commits the necessary changes to the browser DOM.

